{"name":"Haze","hex":"#c8c2c6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Haze","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A diminutive of the female given name Hazel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Haze"}],"entries":[{"title":"Haze","blocks":[{"text":"Haze is traditionally an atmospheric phenomenon in which dust, smoke, and other dry particulates suspended in air obscure visibility and the clarity of the sky. The World Meteorological Organization manual of codes includes a classification of particulates causing horizontal obscuration into categories of fog, ice fog, steam fog, mist, haze, smoke, volcanic ash, dust, sand, and snow. Sources for particles that cause haze include farming, traffic, industry, windy weather, volcanic activity and wildfires.\nSeen from afar and depending on the direction of view with respect to the Sun, haze may appear brownish or bluish, while mist tends to be bluish grey instead. Whereas haze often is considered a phenomenon occurring in dry air, mist formation is a phenomenon in saturated, humid air. However, haze particles may act as condensation nuclei that leads to the subsequent vapor condensation and formation of mist droplets; such forms of haze are known as \"wet haze\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/MosqueinAbuja.jpg/330px-MosqueinAbuja.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haze","wikidata":"Q643546"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg/500px-Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg/1280px-Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg/500px-Striped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Haze over the Mojave Desert from a brush fire in Santa Barbara, California, seen as the Sun descends on the 2016 June solstice, allows the Sun to be photographed without a filter.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStriped_Sun_at_Summer_Solstice_2016.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg/500px-Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg/1280px-Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg/500px-Spooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Haze as smoke pollution over the Mojave from fires in the Inland Empire, June 2016, demonstrates the loss of contrast to the Sun, and the landscape in general.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpooky_Summer_Sunset.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/500px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/1280px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Air_pollution3.jpg/500px-Air_pollution3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAir_pollution3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Sun_during_sunset.jpg/500px-Sun_during_sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Sun_during_sunset.jpg/1280px-Sun_during_sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Sun_during_sunset.jpg/500px-Sun_during_sunset.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The sun viewed directly through a thick haze of atmospheric dust in Meknes, Morocco","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASun_during_sunset.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Mi-14 PŁ Płock 2","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Mi-14_P%C5%81_P%C5%82ock_2.JPG/500px-Mi-14_P%C5%81_P%C5%82ock_2.JPG","ratio":1.998003992015968,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mi-14_P%C5%81_P%C5%82ock_2.JPG","share":0.809375},{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.498125},{"title":"54 Red Mil MI-14 PL HAZE Ukrainian Navy (7724015720)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/54_Red_Mil_MI-14_PL_HAZE_Ukrainian_Navy_%287724015720%29.jpg/500px-54_Red_Mil_MI-14_PL_HAZE_Ukrainian_Navy_%287724015720%29.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:54_Red_Mil_MI-14_PL_HAZE_Ukrainian_Navy_(7724015720).jpg","share":0.3425},{"title":"Öresund bridge in haze","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/%C3%96resund_bridge_in_haze.jpg/500px-%C3%96resund_bridge_in_haze.jpg","ratio":1.7774436090225565,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%96resund_bridge_in_haze.jpg","share":0.310625},{"title":"Mi-14 - odsówane okno","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e0/Mi-14